implementation_summary:
  Rewrote decodedAnswerFindings in src/storytime/book-pictures.ts to design B (owner decision,
  2026-10-27): each text splits at every unescaped double quote into head, every segment between
  two consecutive unescaped quotes, and the tail (including a tail that ends in a lone backslash).
  A tolerant decoder resolves each valid JSON escape, including \uXXXX and surrogate pairs; it
  keeps each invalid escape, lone backslash, and raw control character as literal text; it never
  drops a segment and never throws. Each decoded segment that holds a quote is split and decoded
  again as the next layer; each layer is linear in its length. JSON.parse stays for the review
  schema only. One rule builder serves the raw and decoded scans (RC6-2). The scan position for
  both providers (MiniMax inside the paid callback before the success entry; Kimi before
  parseModelReview and before any record write) is unchanged from task 11. The task 10 refusal
  suffix and the task 9 raw-byte refusal text stay byte-identical. PICTURE_RUBRIC_VERSION, the
  rubric text, and src/song/ are unchanged. No test file changed.

